# Phase 4 — Typing judgments

Add:

```tramaj
require($ctx.title : String)
```

and:

```tramaj
require($ctx : $foo.types.Card)
```

### AST

Something along the lines of:

```text
TypingJudgment
  value: TypedRef
  type: Type
```

where `TypedRef` is intentionally narrower than arbitrary `Expr`.

Initially support:

```text
$ctx
$ctx.foo
$foo.bar
```

and similar statically identifiable paths.

### TODO

* [ ] Parser support for `require(expr : type)`.
* [ ] Desugar/AST representation.
* [ ] Validate that the left side is a supported typing reference.
* [ ] Resolve local type names.
* [ ] Resolve `$foo.types.X`.
* [ ] Add type-checking of field projections.
* [ ] Add errors for unknown types.
* [ ] Add errors for invalid typing targets.
* [ ] Keep typing judgments separate from constraints.

I would **not make `require` a runtime builtin**.

It is analyzer/type-system information.

